---
import { renderToString } from "katex";
import EvidenceDetails from "./EvidenceDetails.astro";
import type { StageView } from "../lib/site-data";
interface Props { view: StageView }
const { view } = Astro.props;
const bridge = view.interludes.find((item) => item.id === "graves-formulation-prerequisite");
if (bridge === undefined) throw new Error("Sutskever needs its Graves formulation prerequisite.");
const math = (value: string) => renderToString(value, { displayMode: true, output: "htmlAndMathml", throwOnError: true });
---
<section class="reading-block alignment-prerequisite" id={bridge.id} aria-labelledby="graves-formulation-heading">
  <p class="kicker">Prerequisite · source formulation</p><h2 id="graves-formulation-heading">Which LSTM does the citation specify?</h2>
  <p>Sutskever et al. name Graves’s 2013 report as the LSTM formulation used. Graves’s canonical v5 presents a later cell with input, forget and output gates and diagonal cell-state-to-gate connections, identifying the 2002 timing paper as its source. The original 1997 cell supplies ancestry; it does not alone specify this later formulation.</p>
  <ol class="copy-path" aria-label="Graves cell update order"><li><strong>Inspect old state</strong><span>Input and forget gates read the previous cell state through coordinatewise connections.</span></li><li><strong>Update the cell</strong><span>Forget scales the old cell; input scales a new candidate. Add the two contributions.</span></li><li><strong>Inspect new state</strong><span>The output gate reads the updated cell; it scales tanh of that cell to produce the hidden output.</span></li></ol>
  {view.mode === "expert" && <>
    <div class="equation-panel" role="region" aria-label="Graves v5 LSTM equations 7 through 11" tabindex="0">
      <div set:html={math(String.raw`i_t=\sigma(W_{xi}x_t+W_{hi}h_{t-1}+W_{ci}c_{t-1}+b_i)`)} />
      <div set:html={math(String.raw`f_t=\sigma(W_{xf}x_t+W_{hf}h_{t-1}+W_{cf}c_{t-1}+b_f)`)} />
      <div set:html={math(String.raw`c_t=f_t\odot c_{t-1}+i_t\odot\tanh(W_{xc}x_t+W_{hc}h_{t-1}+b_c)`)} />
      <div set:html={math(String.raw`o_t=\sigma(W_{xo}x_t+W_{ho}h_{t-1}+W_{co}c_t+b_o),\quad h_t=o_t\odot\tanh(c_t)`)} />
    </div>
    <p>Graves v5 §2.1, article p. 5, Eqs. 7–11. This vector rendering makes coordinatewise products explicit. Wci, Wcf and Wco are diagonal. Graves describes full backpropagation through time and clipping of derivatives. These are the cited source’s equations and training statement; the target translator does not print its full gate implementation. Its own gradient-norm clipping recipe is reported separately below.</p>
  </>}
  <details class="prediction-reveal mt-4"><summary>Check what transfers through the citation</summary><p>The citation identifies a later gated formulation. It does not import Graves’s handwriting window, output mixtures, datasets or results into this translator, or establish every implementation and initialization detail. The future handwriting-window comparison belongs to the alignment chapter.</p></details>
  <p class="mt-3"><a href={`/journeys/recurrent-memory/${view.mode}/hochreiter-schmidhuber-1995-1997/`}>Revisit the original cell</a> · <a href={`/journeys/recurrent-memory/${view.mode}/gers-1999-2000/`}>Revisit forgetting</a> · <a href={`/journeys/recurrent-memory/${view.mode}/gers-2002/`}>Revisit state-to-gate feedback</a></p>
  <a class="claim-link" href="/reference/works/graves-2013-generating-sequences-recurrent-neural-networks/">Inspect Graves’s complete source record</a>
  {bridge.blocks.flatMap((block) => block.evidence).map((evidence) => <EvidenceDetails evidence={evidence} />)}
</section>
